	If you simply want to cause the most damage, you shouldn't be
wielding Magicbane in the first place. There are any number of artifact
weapons out there that are better at doing raw damage, and by the time
you've got the resources that heavily enchanting Magicbane is even an
option, you'll usually have one or more of them.

	My usual weapon strategy for wizards is using Magicbane,
at whatever enchantment it came at, until I get one of the heavy hitters
(and am unrestricted in the appropriate skill by the getting), then
maxing out the enchantment on that and wielding it as primary with
Magicbane on alt for fighting the cursers and casters. After I kill
Rodney, I swap them... Magicbane as primary to resist cursing and switch
to the heavy weapon for major fighting.

